s_rate_neutral":0.7097,"def_epa_per_play":-0.06283}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2024,"team":"SEA","distance":0.4721,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CIN","distance":0.5759,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Zac Taylor"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.6475,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"WAS","distance":0.7127,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"TB","distance":0.7147,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.137,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.1957,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2022,"team":"WAS","distance":0.2806,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.3368,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"WAS","distance":0.3544,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Packers are 4-3 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 145 to 144. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 4th in EPA allowed while the offense sits 16th in EPA per play. Their most distinctive trait is the highest pass rate in the league.","offense":"The Packers offense has been about average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Jordan Love has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Matthew Golden, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Packers have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 5th or better in three of the five main efficiency measures. The one weak spot has been success rate allowed, where they rank 23rd. Lukas Van Ness leads the team with 3.5 sacks, and Edgerrin Cooper has added 3, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 9th highest in the league.","special":"The Packers have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 69% of field goals, which is one of the worst in the league. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Jordan Love has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,958 yards. Matthew Golden has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 540 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by MarShawn Lloyd and Kaleb Johnson. On defense, Lukas Van Ness leads the team with 3.5 sacks and Xavier McKinney has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Matt LaFleur is calling the offense as head coach and Jonathan Gannon is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Seahawks and the 2025 Bengals under Zac Taylor. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Cowboys and the 2023 Panthers under Ejiro Evero.","trends":"The offense went from 4th in EPA per play in 2025 to 16th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 22nd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 4th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was pass rate, which went from 52% to 68%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}